From: Stompers OS <noreply@open-stompers>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: radxa-zero-3w: use the OTG port as a USB device

Put the USB 2.0 OTG Type-C port in peripheral mode so the board shows up
as a USB network and serial gadget when plugged into a computer. The USB 3.0
Type-C port stays a host port.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board configuration]
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3w.dts	2026-10-23 15:13:23.632222576 -0700
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-radxa-zero-3w.dts	2026-10-23 15:13:23.637111478 -0700
@@ -90,3 +90,7 @@
 	uart-has-rtscts;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+&usb_host0_xhci {
+	dr_mode = "peripheral";
+};
